    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Geraghty offer 20 the Village Green to the market, a superbly located, 2-Bedroom mid terrace home with reception room extension, not overlooked front or rear and having a private rear garden.\n\nNo 20 is enviously positioned in the development, is walking distance of Ratoath village center where all amenities are to be had; trendy coffee shops, theatre, supermarkets, a choice of restaurants etc. and is walking distance of schools, both primary and secondary. Avoca garden center and restaurant is a short drive, as is Emerald Park and the Park&Ride facility at M3 Parkway\n\nThe property has been modernized and upgraded and offers hardwood floors downstairs, triple glazed windows and French doors leading to the garden. The kitchen was upgraded in 2018. The accommodation is generous in proportions, and both bedrooms are double in size.\n\nThe property allows easy access to all major road networks via the N2, the N3, the M50 interchange and is on the bus route for Dublin City Centre. \n\nThis lovely extended 2-bedroom home is perfect for those starting out on the property ladder or will suit someone downsizing.\n\nFor transparency purposes, bidding will be carried out online via our unique bidding platform: \"MySherryFitz\" - log on to the sherryfitz website for easy access."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nHardwood front door, timber door with double glazed side panel\n\nGuest WC and WHB - \nTiled floor, extractor fan\n\nSitting Room - \nHardwood floor, fireplace with modern surround, double doors to reception room and stairs to first floor\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - \nKitchen replaced in 2018 having tiled floor, tiling over worktop, extractor hood, integrated dishwasher, plumbed for washing machine and the gas boiler is housed here (original boiler)\n\nReception Room - \nDouble doors from sitting room, hardwood flooring, French doors to garden and the 2 Velux windows allow extra light into this room\n\nFirst Floor - \nCarpet stairs to landing areaAiring Cupboard - pump for showers\n\nBathroom - \nTiled floor, part tiled walls, circular window for light and ventilation\n\nAiring Cupboard - \nPump for shower in main bathroom\n\nBedroom 1 - \nThe main bedroom is positioned at the rear of the residence, has laminate flooring and sliding door wardrobes\n\nEn-Suite Shower Room - \nTiled floor, Mira Elite electric shower (5 years old), and window for natural light and ventilation\n\nBedroom 2 - \nThis double bedroom also has laminate flooring and sliding door wardrobes\n\nExterior - \nSmall, well-tended front gardenVery private rear garden, wall to rear and fence defining neighbouring boundariesGarden shed with electricityParking - not allocated\n\nIncluded in Sale - \nCarpets, window dressings, light fixtures & fittings, ovens, integrated fridge/freezer and garden shed\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Superb location, walking distance of village centre</li><li>Choice of schools close by</li><li>Regular bus service servicing Ashbourne and Dublin City Centre</li><li>Not overlooked front or rear - very private rear garden</li><li>Triple glazed patio doors and windows - 2024</li><li>Kitchen upgraded 2018</li><li>Reception room extension to the rear - 2007, extra insulation installed </li><li>No management Fees</li><li>Parking not allocated</li><li>Mains services, GFCH -original boiler</ul>"
      },
